## 6. Dependency graph and waves

```
Wave 0:  T00 ─┬─ T01   T02   T05        (parallel; T00 first if worktrees are not used)
              │
Wave 1:      T10 ──┬── T11 ──┐
                   ├── T12 ──┼── T15 ──┬── T18 ──┐
                   ├── T13   │   T16   │         ├── T19
                   ├── T14   │   T17 ──┘         │
                   ├── T20 (needs T02, T12)      │
                   └── T30 (persistence, parallel with engine)
Wave 2:      T31 (needs T19, T30) ──┬── T32
                                    ├── T33
                                    └── T34 ──── T35
Wave 3:      T40   T41   T42   T43   T44   (parallel)  ──►  T50, T51  ──► fix loop
```

Maximum parallelism:
- Wave 1 has 6 concurrent agents after T10: T11, T12, T13, T14, T20 and T30. Then T15/T16/T17 run, then T18, then T19.
- Wave 2 has 3 concurrent agents after T31.
- Wave 3 has 5 concurrent agents.

---

## 7. Testing strategy summary

| Layer | Location | Technique | Gate |
|---|---|---|---|
| Unit | `tests/unit` | pytest, builders from T10 | Each task; ≥ 90% line and branch coverage on `engine/` |
| Property | `tests/property` | Hypothesis (`dev` fast, `ci` thorough) | Module invariants (T11–T18) + end-to-end (T41) |
| Acceptance | `tests/acceptance` | Spec scenarios through the public API, written test-first (T05) | All of A01–A21 and A23–A27 green (T40) |
| Services / integration | `tests/services` | Real SQLite (temp file and `:memory:`), fault injection for rollback | Workspace, files, jobs, read models; ≥ 85% coverage on `services/` and `persistence/` |
| CSV | `tests/csv` | Fixture files from T02, round-trip properties | Every documented error code exercised |
| Notebook | `tests/notebook` | `nbclient` execution of `examples/quickstart.ipynb` | Runs clean; key values asserted |
| Performance | `tests/perf` | Generated 1k/10k/50k projects, timed | 10k-task schedule < 2 s and level < 30 s (spec §4.1); misses are reported as defects for triage |
| Static | — | `ruff`, `mypy --strict` | Zero errors on `src/` |

Commands:
- `pytest` (default: unit + property[dev] + acceptance + services + csv)
- `pytest -m notebook`
- `pytest -m perf`
- `pytest --hypothesis-profile=ci`

---

## 8. Definition of done (whole backend phase)

- `pip install -e .` works with zero runtime dependencies. `import project_planner` exposes the §1.2 API.
- All acceptance scenarios in scope pass: A01–A21, A23 (backend part), and A24–A27.
- Property, services, CSV and notebook suites pass; coverage gates are met; `ruff` and `mypy --strict` are clean.
- `docs/decisions.md` has been confirmed by the user, with any overrides applied.
- Calendar parameters, including hours per day and working days per year, are set by the user through calendar initialisation (§2.3). None are hard-coded.
- Time inputs accept hours or days and are never altered. All planning outputs are in days (§2.1). Cost reports show work in the user's choice of person-hours, person-days or person-years (§2.2).
- The performance report exists.
- Spec-conformance and code-review findings are resolved, or explicitly deferred with the user's agreement.
- No module under `engine/` imports `sqlite3`, `services`, `persistence`, or any UI library. This is enforced by a test that inspects imports.
